25637519,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Site-directed mutagenesis and virus production. Eight mutation patterns in RT, including single (D404N, D404E, Y181C and H221Y), double (Y181C/D404N, Y181C/H221Y and D404N/H221Y) and triple (Y181C/D404N/H221Y) mutations, were introduced into the pBRGX plasmid by site-directed mutagenesis as described previously^21 using AccuPrime™ Taq DNA Polymerase High Fidelity (Invitrogen). Details of the amino acid substitutions are listed in Table 1. The presence of mutations in the plasmids was confirmed by DNA sequencing. Constructed mutants and WT plasmids were transfected into 293FT cells in six-well plates uisng Lipofectamine 2000 (Invitrogen) according to the manufacturer's instructions. Seventy-two hours after transfection, the viruses were collected, aliquoted and stored in a –80°C freezer for future use. Viral titre was determined by measuring p24 with a Vironostika kit (bioMérieux, France) and determining the TCID50 in TZM-bl cells as described previously.22 Only those with p24 production >50 mg/L were subjected to phenotypic drug resistance assay and analysis of RC and RT activity. Abstract- Objectives. & Abstract- Conclusions. & Materials and methods- Site-directed mutagenesis and virus production.  & Materials and methods- Phenotypic drug susceptibility of the virus mutants.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It focuses on laboratory-generated mutations and their phenotypic effects.
25637519,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"gag, pol","This work aimed to determine the effects of a novel mutation, D404N, in the connection subdomain of reverse transcriptase (RT). Both pNL-4-3 and infectious pBRGX lentiviral vectors were produced (Gag–Pol) and TZM-bl cells were used to perform phenotypic analyses of drug susceptibility (RT) and viral replication capacity (RC).  Abstract- Objectives. & Materials and methods- Site-directed mutagenesis and virus production.  & Materials and methods- Phenotypic drug susceptibility of the virus mutants.",The paper focuses on the reverse transcriptase (RT) gene of HIV-1. It discusses mutations within the RT gene and their effects on drug resistance and viral replication capacity.
25637519,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Not reported,"Site-directed mutagenesis and virus production. Eight mutation patterns in RT, including single (D404N, D404E, Y181C and H221Y), double (Y181C/D404N, Y181C/H221Y and D404N/H221Y) and triple (Y181C/D404N/H221Y) mutations, were introduced into the pBRGX plasmid by site-directed mutagenesis as described previously21 using AccuPrime™ Taq DNA Polymerase High Fidelity (Invitrogen). Details of the amino acid substitutions are listed in Table 1. The presence of mutations in the plasmids was confirmed by DNA sequencing. Constructed mutants and WT plasmids were transfected into 293FT cells in six-well plates uisng Lipofectamine 2000 (Invitrogen) according to the manufacturer's instructions. Seventy-two hours after transfection, the viruses were collected, aliquoted and stored in a –80°C freezer for future use. Viral titre was determined by measuring p24 with a Vironostika kit (bioMérieux, France) and determining the TCID50 in TZM-bl cells as described previously.22 Only those with p24 production >50 mg/L were subjected to phenotypic drug resistance assay and analysis of RC and RT activity. Abstract- Objectives. & Abstract- Conclusions. & Materials and methods- Site-directed mutagenesis and virus production.  & Materials and methods- Phenotypic drug susceptibility of the virus mutants.",The paper does not specify the sequencing method used. It focuses on the phenotypic effects of the mutations rather than the sequencing process.
25637519,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Not reported,"The WT infectious plasmid pBRGX was constructed and confirmed from a clinical isolate of CRF08_BC subtype in our previous study. The WT infectious plasmid pNL4–3 was constructed based on the pBRGX plasmid. Materials and methods- Cells, plasmids and drugs.",The paper does not mention any specific clinical specimens being sequenced. It focuses on laboratory-generated mutations and their effects on drug resistance and viral replication capacity.
25637519,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"The current study characterized a novel NNRTI-related mutation D404N in RT, which was selected previously by nevirapine during in vitro cell culture. A novel mutation, D404N, in the connection subdomain of reverse transcriptase of HIV-1 CRF08_BC subtype confers cross-resistance to NNRTIs. Materials and methods- Cells, plasmids and drugs. Abstract- Objectives.",The paper focuses on laboratory-generated mutations and does not mention obtaining sequences from individuals with virological failure.
