29373677,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"In this study, we report the case of a patient treated with dolutegravir monotherapy. Identification of N155H, K156N, K211R and E212T mutations in a patient failing dolutegravir treatment.","The paper discusses the case of a patient treated with dolutegravir monotherapy and mentions the identification of specific mutations in the HIV-1 integrase gene from this patient, indicating that HIV sequences were reported."
29373677,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"The impact of N155H-K156N-K211R-E212T mutations was studied in cell-free, culture-based assays and by molecular modelling. Dolutegravir, an integrase strand-transfer inhibitor (STI), shows a high genetic barrier to resistance. We first investigated the replicative properties of mutant viruses. The patient infected with a B subtype HIV-1 strain received an antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, a period during which CD4 counts had increased from 350 to 940 cells/mm3. Virus infections. Infections were performed on MT4 cells (2 × 106 cells/mL with 20 ng of p24gag antigen per 106 cells) with or without drugs. Four hours post-infection, cells were washed in PBS and new medium was added. At various times post-infection, 1–2 million cells were harvested and dry pellets were frozen at –80°C.","The study investigates the susceptibility of HIV-1 integrase mutants to dolutegravir and raltegravir in both cell-free and culture-based assays, indicating that in vitro drug susceptibility data is reported."
29373677,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"We first investigated the replicative properties of mutant viruses. The patient infected with a B subtype HIV-1 strain received an antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, a period during which CD4 counts had increased from 350 to 940 cells/mm3. Virus infections. Infections were performed on MT4 cells (2 × 106 cells/mL with 20 ng of p24gag antigen per 106 cells) with or without drugs. Four hours post-infection, cells were washed in PBS and new medium was added. At various times post-infection, 1–2 million cells were harvested and dry pellets were frozen at –80°C.","The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers or public availability of the reported sequences, focusing instead on the case study of a single patient."
