29373677,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Not reported,"The patient infected with a B subtype HIV-1 strain received an antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, a period during which CD4 counts had increased from 350 to 940 cells/mm3. Virus infections. Infections were performed on MT4 cells (2 × 106 cells/mL with 20 ng of p24gag antigen per 106 cells) with or without drugs. Four hours post-infection, cells were washed in PBS and new medium was added. At various times post-infection, 1–2 million cells were harvested and dry pellets were frozen at –80°C.","The paper does not mention the specific countries from which the sequenced samples were obtained, focusing instead on the patient's clinical history."
29373677,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2008 to 2015,"The patient infected with a B subtype HIV-1 strain received an antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, a period during which CD4 counts had increased from 350 to 940 cells/mm3. Virus infections. Infections were performed on MT4 cells (2 × 106 cells/mL with 20 ng of p24gag antigen per 106 cells) with or without drugs. Four hours post-infection, cells were washed in PBS and new medium was added. At various times post-infection, 1–2 million cells were harvested and dry pellets were frozen at –80°C.","The paper states that the patient received antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, during which the HIV-1 integrase mutations were analyzed."
29373677,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"We first investigated the replicative properties of mutant viruses. The patient infected with a B subtype HIV-1 strain received an antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, a period during which CD4 counts had increased from 350 to 940 cells/mm3. Virus infections. Infections were performed on MT4 cells (2 × 106 cells/mL with 20 ng of p24gag antigen per 106 cells) with or without drugs. Four hours post-infection, cells were washed in PBS and new medium was added. At various times post-infection, 1–2 million cells were harvested and dry pellets were frozen at –80°C.","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing, focusing instead on the analysis of mutations in the patient's HIV-1 integrase gene."
29373677,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,IN gene,"In this study, we report the case of a patient treated with dolutegravir monotherapy. Identification of N155H, K156N, K211R and E212T mutations in a patient failing dolutegravir treatment. Our data indicate that the in trans IN mutants of the N155H-K156N-K211R-E212T pathway cannot be resistant to dolutegravir.","The paper focuses on the sequencing and mutation analysis of the HIV-1 integrase (IN) gene, specifically discussing several mutations in this gene."
29373677,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Not reported,"We first investigated the replicative properties of mutant viruses. The patient infected with a B subtype HIV-1 strain received an antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, a period during which CD4 counts had increased from 350 to 940 cells/mm3. Virus infections. Infections were performed on MT4 cells (2 × 106 cells/mL with 20 ng of p24gag antigen per 106 cells) with or without drugs. Four hours post-infection, cells were washed in PBS and new medium was added. At various times post-infection, 1–2 million cells were harvested and dry pellets were frozen at –80°C.","The paper does not specify the sequencing method used, focusing instead on the mutations observed and the susceptibility assays performed."
29373677,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma RNA and DNA from PBMCs,"Integrase genotypic analysis was performed on DNA from PBMCs, when the plasma viral load was below 20 copies/mL and on plasma RNA when it was detectable above 20 copies/mL. Single-cycle titres of the virus were determined on HeLa-P4 cells as previously described. Cells were infected in 96-well plates (3 ng of p24gag antigen) with or without raltegravir or dolutegravir. Viral titre was determined by quantifying β-galactosidase activity in HeLa-P4 lysates using a colorimetric assay.","The paper describes the analysis of HIV-1 integrase mutations in DNA from PBMCs and plasma RNA, indicating that both types of samples were sequenced."
29373677,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Failure of dolutegravir treatment was observed concomitant with the appearance of N155H-K211R-E212T mutations in the integrase (IN) gene in addition to the polymorphic K156N mutation that was present at baseline in this patient. Identification of N155H, K156N, K211R and E212T mutations in a patient failing dolutegravir treatment.","The paper discusses a patient who experienced virological failure while on dolutegravir monotherapy, and mutations were identified during this failure."
29373677,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"In this study, we report the case of a patient treated with dolutegravir monotherapy. Failure of dolutegravir treatment was observed concomitant with the appearance of N155H-K211R-E212T mutations in the integrase (IN) gene in addition to the polymorphic K156N mutation that was present at baseline in this patient.","The paper details a case study of a single patient treated with dolutegravir monotherapy, and does not mention the individual being part of a clinical trial."
29373677,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"The patient infected with a B subtype HIV-1 strain received an antiretroviral treatment including INSTIs from 2008 to 2015, a period during which CD4 counts had increased from 350 to 940 cells/mm3. The patient was first treated with raltegravir in combination with tenofovir/emtricitabine (Truvada) for 6 years until 2014, during which time the viral load remained undetectable (plasma HIV RNA <20 copies/mL). Every 6 months, during follow-up, genotypic analysis of integrase was tested in DNA and never showed any mutations selected against raltegravir. Owing to treatment intolerance, a simplification of treatment with dolutegravir monotherapy (not currently recommended in any guidelines for HIV-1 treatment) was proposed to the patient in 2014 while the viral load was still undetectable. Five months later, the viral load became detectable in plasma at 291 copies/mL.","The paper mentions that the patient had received previous antiretroviral treatments, including INSTIs, before the sample for HIV sequencing was obtained."
29373677,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI, II","The patient was first treated with raltegravir in combination with tenofovir/emtricitabine (Truvada) for 6 years until 2014, during which time the viral load remained undetectable (plasma HIV RNA <20 copies/mL). Every 6 months, during follow-up, genotypic analysis of integrase was tested in DNA and never showed any mutations selected against raltegravir. Owing to treatment intolerance, a simplification of treatment with dolutegravir monotherapy (not currently recommended in any guidelines for HIV-1 treatment) was proposed to the patient in 2014 while the viral load was still undetectable. Five months later, the viral load became detectable in plasma at 291 copies/mL.","The paper mentions that the patient received a combination therapy of NRTI (tenofovir/emtricitabine), PI (Protenevir), II (raltegravir and dolutegravir), and non-nukesabl RTIs (etravirine)."
29373677,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Tenofovir, Emtricitabine, Raltegravir, Dolutegravir, Etravirine, Saquinavir Findriss.","The patient was first treated with raltegravir in combination with tenofovir/emtricitabine (Truvada) for 6 years until 2014, during which time the viral load remained undetectable (plasma HIV RNA <20 copies/mL). Every 6 months, during follow-up, genotypic analysis of integrase was tested in DNA and never showed any mutations selected against raltegravir. Owing to treatment intolerance, a simplification of treatment with dolutegravir monotherapy (not currently recommended in any guidelines for HIV-1 treatment) was proposed to the patient in 2014 while the viral load was still undetectable. Five months later, the viral load became detectable in plasma at 291 copies/mL.","The paper mentions that the patient received treatments with various drugs, including raltegravir(RAL), Emtricitabine + Tenofovir (EFV), Saquinavir (SQV), Etravirine (ETR), and Dolutegravir (DTG)."
30053052,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"Stored plasma samples from patients who were either therapy naive (n = 42) or had a virological treatment failure (n = 9) were randomly selected from the HIV cohort at Karolinska University Hospital, Stockholm, Sweden. Of these, 11 samples did not give any positive clones even after multiple efforts, and 13 were not replication competent. Finally we obtained 24 replication-competent viruses from treatment-naive individuals who were pure subtypes (HIV-1A1, n = 1; HIV-1B, n = 5; HIV-1C, n = 15) or circulating recombinant forms (CRFs) (01_AE, n = 1; 02_AG, n = 2), whilst the viruses extracted from patients with therapy failure (n = 3) were HIV-1B (n = 1), HIV-1D (n = 1) and HIV-1C (n = 1), as determined by our previously published near full-length sequencing protocol.","The paper mentions that stored plasma samples from patients who were either therapy naive or had a virological treatment failure were randomly selected from the HIV cohort at Karolinska University Hospital, Stockholm, Sweden. This indicates that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
30053052,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,Methods. pNL4.3 chimeric viruses encoding gag-pol from treatment-naive patients (n = 24) and therapy-failure patients (n = 3) and a panel of reverse transcriptase inhibitor-resistant strains (n = 7) were used to compare the potency of reverse transcriptase inhibitor drugs. The phenotypic drug susceptibility assay was performed using TZM-bl cells. In vitro inhibition assays were done using patient-derived reverse transcriptase. IC50 values of NNRTIs were calculated using a PicoGreen-based spectrophotometric assay. Steady-state kinetics were used to determine the apparent binding affinity (Km.dNTP) of triphosphate form of EFdA (EFdA-TP) and dATP.,"The paper describes several assays to test the effectiveness of different drugs against HIV-1 viruses, including chimeric viruses and drug-resistant strains. The use of TZM-bl cells and assays to measure IC50 values and binding affinities indicates that in vitro drug susceptibility data were generated."
