30053052,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,Yes,"The gag-pol fragment (HXB2: 0702-5798) was cloned into pNL43 plasmid following digestion with BssHII and SalI (New England Biolabs, USA) and ligation using T4 DNA ligase (New England Biolabs), as described by us previously. The chimeric viruses were produced by transient transfection of the plasmids into the 293 T cell line using FuGENE® HD Transfection Reagent (Promega, USA) and harvested 72 h later by collection of the cell-free supernatant via centrifugation; aliquots were stored at −80°C.",The paper describes the construction of chimeric viruses by cloning the gag-pol fragment into the pNL43 plasmid. This indicates that samples were cloned prior to sequencing.
