31988104,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No.,"The susceptibilities to antiviral drugs of site-directed mutants (SDMs) and patient-derived mutants containing combinations of TAMs (M41L, D67N, K70R, L210W, T215Y, and K219Q) with or without the M184V mutation (TAMs±M184V) were evaluated using either 5-day multicycle (MC; n = 110) or 2-day single-cycle (SC; n = 96) HIV assays.","The paper does not mention any sequences from patient samples; instead, it focuses on site-directed mutants and their susceptibility to antiviral drugs."
31988104,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes.,"Comparative susceptibility of TAF and TDF against HIV-1 site-directed mutants carrying TAMs with (M184V) or without the M184V mutation was performed in 2-day single-cycle and 5-day multicycle assay formats. The single-cycle assay determines virus yield in the absence of drug over a 2-day period, and the different drug concentrations in the assay reflect the intracellular concentration of drug achieved clinically six hours post-dose with the exception of the resistance buffer assay described below that mimics intracellular concentrations achieved 2 hours post-dose.",The paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data through phenotypic and viral breakthrough assays with HIV-1 mutants and patient-derived isolates.
31988104,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No.,"The susceptibilities to antiviral drugs of site-directed mutants (SDMs) and patient-derived mutants containing combinations of TAMs (M41L, D67N, K70R, L210W, T215Y, and K219Q) with or without the M184V mutation (TAMs±M184V) were evaluated using either 5-day multicycle (MC; n = 110) or 2-day single-cycle (SC; n = 96) HIV assays.",The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers or public availability of sequences; it focuses on pharmacological studies.
