34516245,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"To study EFdA resistance patterns that may emerge in naive or tenofovir (TFV)-, emtricitabine/lamivudine (FTC/3TC)-, or zidovudine (AZT)-treated patients, we performed viral passaging experiments starting with WT, K65R, M184V, or D67N/K70R/T215F/K219Q HIV-1. Using recombinant viruses, we validated the role for M184V as the primary determinant of EFdA resistance; none of the observed connection subdomain (R358K and E399K) or RNase H domain (A502V) mutations significantly contributed to EFdA resistance.","The paper focuses on viral passaging experiments and the use of recombinant viruses, not patient samples, so it does not report sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
34516245,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not reported,"To study EFdA resistance patterns that may emerge in naive or tenofovir (TFV)-, emtricitabine/lamivudine (FTC/3TC)-, or zidovudine (AZT)-treated patients, we performed viral passaging experiments starting with WT, K65R, M184V, or D67N/K70R/T215F/K219Q HIV-1. Using recombinant viruses, we validated the role for M184V as the primary determinant of EFdA resistance; none of the observed connection subdomain (R358K and E399K) or RNase H domain (A502V) mutations significantly contributed to EFdA resistance.","The paper focuses on viral passaging experiments and the use of recombinant viruses, and although it mentions the effects of certain drugs on HIV sequences, there is no indication that samples were obtained from individuals who had received ARV drugs before sequencing."
34516245,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not reported,"To study EFdA resistance patterns that may emerge in naive or tenofovir (TFV)-, emtricitabine/lamivudine (FTC/3TC)-, or zidovudine (AZT)-treated patients, we performed viral passaging experiments starting with WT, K65R, M184V, or D67N/K70R/T215F/K219Q HIV-1. Using recombinant viruses, we validated the role for M184V as the primary determinant of EFdA resistance; none of the observed connection subdomain (R358K and E399K) or RNase H domain (A502V) mutations significantly contributed to EFdA resistance.","The paper focuses on viral passaging experiments and the use of recombinant viruses, and while it mentions the drugs used in the experiments (EFdA, tenofovir, FTC, and AZT), there is no mention of samples from individuals who received these drugs before the sequencing."
35730213,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"HIV programmes across many countries in Africa have recently transitioned people living with HIV from efavirenz (EFV)- to dolutegravir (DTG)-containing antiretroviral therapy (ART). As both drugs are associated with neuropsychiatric adverse effects, this study assessed the mental health and HIV/ART-associated symptoms of people living with HIV before and after transition to DTG.","The paper focuses on the mental health and HIV/ART-associated symptoms of individuals transitioning from efavirenz to dolutegravir-based ART. It does not mention any sequencing of HIV samples from patients, nor does it discuss HIV sequences or their publication in databases like GenBank."
35730213,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"HIV programmes across many countries in Africa have recently transitioned people living with HIV from efavirenz (EFV)- to dolutegravir (DTG)-containing antiretroviral therapy (ART). As both drugs are associated with neuropsychiatric adverse effects, this study assessed the mental health and HIV/ART-associated symptoms of people living with HIV before and after transition to DTG.","The content of the paper does not include any mention of in vitro drug susceptibility data. It primarily discusses the transition between antiretroviral therapies and their effects on mental health and physical well-being, not on the susceptibility of HIV to drugs in vitro."
35730213,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"HIV programmes across many countries in Africa have recently transitioned people living with HIV from efavirenz (EFV)- to dolutegravir (DTG)-containing antiretroviral therapy (ART). As both drugs are associated with neuropsychiatric adverse effects, this study assessed the mental health and HIV/ART-associated symptoms of people living with HIV before and after transition to DTG.","The paper does not mention any sequences obtained from patient samples, nor does it discuss the public availability of such sequences. The study focuses on the mental health outcomes of transitioning ART regimens rather than on genetic sequencing."
35730213,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No GenBank accession numbers reported,"HIV programmes across many countries in Africa have recently transitioned people living with HIV from efavirenz (EFV)- to dolutegravir (DTG)-containing antiretroviral therapy (ART). As both drugs are associated with neuropsychiatric adverse effects, this study assessed the mental health and HIV/ART-associated symptoms of people living with HIV before and after transition to DTG.",The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates because it does not report any sequencing data at all. The focus is on the effects of ART on mental health rather than on viral genotyping.
