35730213,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,NRTI and NNRTI,"Of the 1,228 DO-REAL participants included in this analysis, 222 (18%) were ART-naïve at study entry, and 1,006 (82%) were ART-experienced. Among the 1,006 ART-experienced people, the majority (98%) were receiving a backbone of tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (tenofovir DF; TDF) plus lamivudine (3TC) or emtricitabine (FTC) (91% of whom were receiving TDF/3TC) curated from patient records. A total of 571/1006 (57%) were on an efavirenz-based regimen: EFV/TDF/3TC (n=549; 96%) or EFV/TDF/FTC (n=22; 4%).",The study mentions that the participants were on a tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) and lamivudine (3TC)/efavirenz (EFV) based regimen which are part of the NRTI and NNRTI drug classes.
35730213,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"TDF, 3TC, EFV","Of the 1,228 DO-REAL participants included in this analysis, 222 (18%) were ART-naïve at study entry, and 1,006 (82%) were ART-experienced. Among the 1,006 ART-experienced people, the majority (98%) were receiving a backbone of tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (tenofovir DF; TDF) plus lamivudine (3TC) or emtricitabine (FTC) (91% of whom were receiving TDF/3TC) curated from patient records. A total of 571/1006 (57%) were on an efavirenz-based regimen: EFV/TDF/3TC (n=549; 96%) or EFV/TDF/FTC (n=22; 4%).","The paper specifies that participants were on a regimen of tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF), lamivudine (3TC), and efavirenz (EFV) before transitioning to dolutegravir (DTG)."
35913500,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"First Demonstration Project of Long-Acting Injectable Antiretroviral Therapy for Persons With and Without Detectable Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) Viremia in an Urban HIV Clinic;Methods
Ward 86 is a large HIV clinic in San Francisco that serves publicly insured and underinsured patients. We started patients on LAI-ART via a structured process of provider referral, multidisciplinary review (MD, RN, pharmacist), and monitoring for on-time injections. Inclusion criteria were willingness to receive monthly injections and a reliable contact method.
Results
Between June 2021 and April 2022, 51 patients initiated LAI-ART, with 39 receiving at least 2 follow-up injections by database closure (median age, 46 years; 90% cisgender men, 61% non-White, 41% marginally housed, 54% currently using stimulants). Of 24 patients who initiated injections with viral suppression (median CD4 cell count, 706 cells/mm3), 100% (95% confidence interval [CI], 86%–100%) maintained viral suppression. Of 15 patients who initiated injections with detectable viremia (median CD4 cell count, 99 cells/mm3; mean log10 viral load, 4.67; standard deviation, 1.16), 12 (80%; 95% CI, 55%–93%) achieved viral suppression, and the other 3 had a 2-log viral load decline by a median of 22 days.
Conclusions
This small demonstration project of LAI-ART in a diverse group of patients with high levels of substance use and marginal housing demonstrated promising early treatment outcomes, including in those with detectable viremia due to adherence challenges. More data on LAI-ART in hard-to-reach populations are needed.","The paper does not mention any sequencing of HIV from patient samples, nor does it discuss any data related to HIV sequences. The focus is on the implementation and outcomes of a long-acting injectable antiretroviral therapy program for individuals with varying levels of HIV viremia, but it does not provide any information about sequencing or genetic analysis of HIV."
