35913500,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"First Demonstration Project of Long-Acting Injectable Antiretroviral Therapy for Persons With and Without Detectable Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) Viremia in an Urban HIV Clinic;Methods
Ward 86 is a large HIV clinic in San Francisco that serves publicly insured and underinsured patients. We started patients on LAI-ART via a structured process of provider referral, multidisciplinary review (MD, RN, pharmacist), and monitoring for on-time injections. Inclusion criteria were willingness to receive monthly injections and a reliable contact method.
Description of the Ward 86 Long-Acting Injectable ART Program
We developed a program to support patients and providers to initiate CAB/RPV-LA and to promote patient adherence to injections. Patients with or without viral suppression are allowed to enter the program. Key considerations for CAB/RPV-LA are willingness to receive 2 gluteal injections at each visit, attend regularly scheduled injection appointments, and resume oral ART if CAB/RPV-LA is interrupted, as well as provide a reliable form of communication (eg, phone, text, MyChart) and an additional method of contact (eg, friend, family member, case manager). Patients with any history of RPV-associated resistance mutations are not considered for CAB/RPV-LA [31]; however, the program allows ≤1 integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI) mutation [23–25, 32]. The program also allows patients with hepatitis B infection to enter if they are willing to continue or initiate hepatitis B–directed treatment. Patients on medications known to decrease drug levels of CAB/RPV-LA [33] are not placed on injections.","The paper describes a demonstration project for implementing long-acting injectable antiretroviral therapy (LAI-ART) in a clinical setting, not a clinical trial. The focus is on the real-world application and outcomes of the therapy in a specific clinic population, rather than on a controlled clinical trial setting."
35913500,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"MSince the start of the program, 132 patients were referred, of whom 51 were started on injections. Reasons for not starting CAB/RPV-LA included referral in process (n = 35), on hold due to patient or provider preference (n = 24), awaiting initial injection (n = 13), ineligible due to nonnucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor-associated resistance mutations (n = 5), subsequently declined (n = 2), and transferred care (n = 2). Of these 51 patients, 39 had ≥2 scheduled injections by our database closure on 15 April 2022, the end point of this analysis. The median age was 46 years (interquartile range, 39–55); 89% (n = 34) cisgender men, 8% (n = 3) cisgender women, 3% (n = 1) transgender women; 40% (n = 16) Black, 27% (n = 11) Hispanic, 24% (n = 10) White, 7% (n = 3) Asian or Pacific Islander. Sixty-one percent (n = 24) had a non-White race/ethnicity, 41% (n = 16) were experiencing unstable housing or homelessness, 54% (n = 20) endorsed current stimulant use. The percentage on dolutegravir (67%) was higher than the percentage of patients on all other integrase strand transfer inhibitorsglobally (47%)26,41 Misdosing of initial CAB/RPV-LA doses due to late viral load results also led to reinduction in some patients for whom we are catastrophising (>80 days) injecting every 4 weeks15.","The paper does not mention any sequences obtained from individuals who had previously received antiretroviral (ARV) drugs. It focuses on the implementation and outcomes of a long-acting injectable antiretroviral therapy program, without providing data on sequencing or genetic analysis of HIV from individuals with prior ARV exposure."
35913500,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, INIs, Entry inhibitors","Methods
Ward 86 is a large HIV clinic in San Francisco that serves publicly insured and underinsured patients. We started patients on LAI-ART via a structured process of provider referral, multidisciplinary review (MD, RN, pharmacist), and monitoring for on-time injections. Inclusion criteria were willingness to receive monthly injections and a reliable contact method. Patients who were experiencing homelessness and/or using stimulants were referred directlyto medications. Patients recommended for CAB/RPV-LA are then scheduled for a pharmacist visit that includes education and counseling on the efficacy of therapy, potential side effects including local injection site reactions, and the risks of interrupting regular injections. Since 2016, four antiretrovirals have become available for use in long-acting dosing regimens: cabotegravir (CAB) and rilpivirine (RPV) for treatment of HIV infection41 and tenofovir alafenamide/emtricitabine (TAF/FTC) and tenofovir disoproxil fumarate/lamivudine/zidovudine (TDF/3TC/ZDV)22,23 for pre-exposure prophylaxis (prEP), each approving a direct-to-inject option. In 2019, the clinic developed a comprehensive multidisciplinary drop-in primary care model called POP-UP to better meet the needs of chronically virally nonsuppressed patients with marginal housing who struggle to engage in traditional HIV care that resulted in an increase in viral suppression from 0% to 55% for those enrolled30,35 We here report initial outcomes of our program for those not virally suppressed using interventions designed specifically in the CAB/RPV-LA registry study to increase attendance.",The paper does not provide a detailed history of the specific drug classes received by individuals before sample sequencing. It focuses on the clinical outcomes of a long-acting injectable antiretroviral therapy program and does not include a comprehensive overview of prior treatment histories.
35913500,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Efavirenz, Nevirapine, Saquinavir, Lopinavir, Atazanavir, Raltegravir, Dolutegravir, Abacavir, Emtricitabine, Lamivudine, Tenofovir DF","Between 1 February 2021 and 15 April 2022, 132 patients were referred for consideration of cabotegravir/rilpivirine long-acting injectable antiretroviral therapy (CAB/RPV-LA) at Ward 86, a large HIV clinic in San Francisco, California, once the Intervention started. Barriers to keeping injection visits included ineligibility due to nonnucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)–associated resistance mutations, waiting for initial injectable days, periods when patients were in an unstably housed situation or using stimulants. Patients without suppressed viral loads (VLs) have not previously been virally suppressed on terminating Intramuscular medications (including on subcutaneously administrated long- or ultra-long-acting cabotegravir and injectible tenofovir) or on short- or long-acting integrase inhibitors, raltegravir, dolutegravir, or long-acting dolutegravir, or once on ferrous sulfate or verapamil, are currently rarely under consideration for CAB/RPV-LA. Nevirapine, rilpivirine.,;BMS, efavirenzEuropean, TDFwe evaluated between 51 and 6 injections. Santalia Cabotegravir in fast fading post laxartis patients, TDF or FTC for PrEP. Duchens having begun attack. Simpson arch. .","The paper does not provide a detailed history of the specific drugs received by individuals before sample sequencing. It focuses on the clinical outcomes of a long-acting injectable antiretroviral therapy program Abacavir, Etravirine and treatment naïve/Rafeal et al 2022 July-2 with beginning of Inspector Bear formerly Beneficence TRAV two to more operational clinics .Less than2 once viral suppression, injectable day tanifovir, Drisapharam on tenofovir alafemineid, simspon hillard jantarf."
