36659824,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. No emergent resistance-associated mutations were detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48.,"The paper discusses the results of a clinical trial involving the initiation of a specific HIV treatment regimen and its outcomes on viral load and resistance mutations but does not indicate that actual HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples. Specifically, it mentions the absence of detected resistance mutations but does not provide details on sequencing or sequence availability, focusing instead on clinical outcomes and safety of the treatment regimen."
36659824,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. Virological non-response was defined as a pVL≥400 copies/mL at the W12 visit, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later, or as a pVL≥50 copies/mL at the W24 visit or thereafter, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later. In such cases, National French Guidelines also recommended performance of a resistance genotypic test and determination of BIC, FTC and tenofovir (TFV) plasma concentrations. Virological non-response was defined as a pVL≥400 copies/mL at the W12 visit, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later, or as a pVL≥50 copies/mL at the W24 visit or thereafter, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later. In such cases, National French Guidelines also recommended performance of a resistance genotypic test and determination of BIC, FTC and tenofovir (TFV) plasma concentrations. This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing or results. It focuses on clinical outcomes, safety, and pharmacological analysis of a specific treatment regimen for HIV, without discussing any laboratory data related to drug susceptibility testing."
36659824,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. Virological non-response was defined as a pVL≥400 copies/mL at the W12 visit, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later, or as a pVL≥50 copies/mL at the W24 visit or thereafter, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later. In such cases, National French Guidelines also recommended performance of a resistance genotypic test and determination of BIC, FTC and tenofovir (TFV) plasma concentrations. Virological non-response was defined as a pVL≥400 copies/mL at the W12 visit, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later, or as a pVL≥50 copies/mL at the W24 visit or thereafter, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later. In such cases, National French Guidelines also recommended performance of a resistance genotypic test and determination of BIC, FTC and tenofovir (TFV) plasma concentrations. This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.",The paper does not provide any information regarding the public availability of sequences. It focuses on the clinical outcomes and safety of the treatment regimen without mentioning any data sharing or deposition in public databases.
36659824,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. Virological non-response was defined as a pVL≥400 copies/mL at the W12 visit, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later, or as a pVL≥50 copies/mL at the W24 visit or thereafter, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later. In such cases, National French Guidelines also recommended performance of a resistance genotypic test and determination of BIC, FTC and tenofovir (TFV) plasma concentrations. Virological non-response was defined as a pVL≥400 copies/mL at the W12 visit, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later, or as a pVL≥50 copies/mL at the W24 visit or thereafter, confirmed on a second sample taken 2--3 weeks later. In such cases, National French Guidelines also recommended performance of a resistance genotypic test and determination of BIC, FTC and tenofovir (TFV) plasma concentrations. This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.",The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates. It discusses the clinical outcomes of a treatment regimen without providing specific sequence data or accession information.
36659824,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. The protocol-defined virological failure (PDVF, 2 consecutive pVL≥50 copies/mL as of W24) was observed in 11/112 (9.8%) at W24 and 14/112 (12.5%) at W48. This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper mentions the inclusion of 112 participants in the treatment analysis but does not specify the number of individuals from whom samples were obtained for HIV sequencing. It focuses on the clinical outcomes of the treatment regimen, and the mention of genotypic resistance tests doesn't imply sequencing of all participants."
36659824,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,No,"One hundred and eighteen participants were enrolled across 15 sites in France between November 2019 and September 2020. Six had protocol violation: three false-positive HIV tests [one self-test and two HIV immunoassay (ELISA 4th generation) tests], one already in medical care, two pretreated). Thus, 112 were included in the ITT-FDA Snapshot analysis (see flow chart, Figure 1).","The paper focuses on a clinical study conducted in France, and while it discusses the demographics of the participants, it does not provide any information about the countries from which sequenced samples were obtained, nor does it indicate that samples were sequenced."
36659824,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,No,"One hundred and eighteen participants were enrolled across 15 sites in France between November 2019 and September 2020. Six had protocol violation: three false-positive HIV tests [one self-test and two HIV immunoassay (ELISA 4th generation) tests], one already in medical care, two pretreated). Thus, 112 were included in the ITT-FDA Snapshot analysis (see flow chart, Figure 1).","The paper does not provide any information regarding the years from which sequenced samples were obtained, as it does not report any sequencing data."
36659824,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. Participants had to be ART-naive, and to have minimally symptomatic HIV infection (World Health Organisation clinical stage I--I). This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing, as it does not report any sequencing data."
36659824,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. Participants had to be ART-naive, and to have minimally symptomatic HIV infection (World Health Organisation clinical stage I--I). This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper does not mention any specific HIV genes that were sequenced, as it does not report any sequencing data."
36659824,10,What method was used for sequencing?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. Participants had to be ART-naive, and to have minimally symptomatic HIV infection (World Health Organisation clinical stage I--I). This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper does not mention any sequencing methods, as it does not report any sequencing data."
36659824,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,No,"No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. Participants had to be ART-naive, and to have minimally symptomatic HIV infection (World Health Organisation clinical stage I--I). This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper does not specify any type of clinical specimens that were sequenced, as it does not report any sequencing data."
36659824,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"Overall, 112 participants were included in the ITT population. During follow-up, seven participants discontinued the study drug but remained on the study, and seven others discontinued follow-up. According to FDA Snapshot analysis, at W24 and W48, 90/112, (80.4%; 95% CI: 71.8--87.3) and 95/112 (84.8%; 95% CI: 76.8--90.9) of participants achieved pVL < 50 copies/mL, respectively. The protocol-defined virological failure (PDVF, 2 consecutive pVL ≥ 50 copies/mL as of W24) was observed in 11/112 (9.8%) at W24 and 14/112 (12.5%) at W48. No emergent resistance-associated mutation was detected in those with PDVF at W24 and W48. This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.",The paper mentions that the virological failure was observed in 11/112 at W24 but not mentioned that blood samples were sequenced.
36659824,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"The FAST study was a national, multicentre, prospective, open-label single-arm study assessing the feasibility, efficacy and safety of BIC/FTC/TAF in a same-day initiation model. This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper describes the FAST study as a national, multicenter, prospective, open-label single-arm clinical trial, indicating that the patients were part of a clinical trial."
36659824,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"Participants had to be ART-naive, and to have minimally symptomatic HIV infection (World Health Organisation clinical stage I--I). This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper mentioned that the participants were ART-naive,  all treatment-emergent HIV resistance-associated mutations concerned baseline resistance mutations, no new resistance mutations emerged during treatment, which means baseline resistance samples were sequenced but not treatment-emergent ones. So the answer is No."
36659824,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No,"Participants had to be ART-naive, and to have minimally symptomatic HIV infection (World Health Organisation clinical stage I--I). This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper mentioned that the participants were ART-naive,  all treatment-emergent HIV resistance-associated mutations concerned baseline resistance mutations, no new resistance mutations emerged during treatment, which means baseline resistance samples were sequenced but not treatment-emergent ones. So according to the sequences from the study, they had not received any drugs from any classes before sample sequencing."
36659824,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No,"Participants had to be ART-naive, and to have minimally symptomatic HIV infection (World Health Organisation clinical stage I--I). This study was funded by Gilead Sciences. The funder had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.","The paper mentioned that the participants were ART-naive,  all treatment-emergent HIV resistance-associated mutations concerned baseline resistance mutations, no new resistance mutations emerged during treatment, which means baseline resistance samples were sequenced but not treatment-emergent ones. So according to the sequences from the study, they had not received any drugs before sample sequencing."
36660819,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"This study does not report specific HIV sequences from patient samples, as it focuses on the evaluation of a long-acting antiretroviral regimen's efficacy and safety in maintaining HIV-1 virologic suppression.","The paper primarily discusses the results of the ATLAS-2M study, which evaluates the efficacy and safety of cabotegravir and rilpivirine in maintaining virologic suppression, but does not mention the sequencing of HIV samples from patients."
