37071019,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,The paper focuses on laboratory studies involving recombinant HIV-1 integrase proteins and cell-based assays to analyze resistance and fitness of specific integrase mutations. It does not mention obtaining HIV sequences from patient samples or provide any related data.,The content primarily discusses the effects of integrase mutations on drug resistance and viral fitness using laboratory assays and does not include any mention of patient-derived sequences.
37071019,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"The study uses cell-based infectivity, replicative capacity, and resistance assays to evaluate the susceptibility of HIV-1 strains with specific integrase mutations to the drugs dolutegravir (DTG) and bictegravir (BIC). It reports detailed measurements of resistance levels for these drugs against the mutations G118R and R263K.","The paper includes in vitro drug susceptibility data by performing resistance assays with DTG and BIC on HIV-1 strains carrying the G118R and R263K mutations, documenting the fold changes in susceptibility compared to wild-type strains."
37071019,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers or indicate that sequences were deposited in a public database. It primarily discusses laboratory findings related to recombinant proteins and assays without mentioning public availability of sequences.,There is no mention of publicly available sequences or data deposits in GenBank within the content of the paper.
37071019,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,None,"The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates, as it does not report any patient samples or sequencing data.","The study does not involve sequencing of HIV isolates, therefore no GenBank accession numbers are provided."
37071019,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,0,"The paper does not report any individuals from whom samples were obtained for HIV sequencing, as it focuses on laboratory assays and recombinant proteins.","The study does not mention any individuals or patient samples, focusing instead on in vitro assays and cell-based experiments."
