37537871,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"Protease, Reverse Transcriptase, Integrase","Protease and reverse transcriptase nucleotide sequences were determined by our in-house Sanger sequencing-based genotypic resistance test ( 18 ), whereas the sequences of integrase were characterized by another in-house Sanger sequencing protocol developed by our team ( 19 ).","The paper mentions that genotypic resistance tests were performed on the protease and reverse transcriptase (RT) genes, and the integrase gene was characterized by Sanger sequencing."
37537871,10,What method was used for sequencing?,"Sanger sequencing, Illumina sequencing, ONT sequencing","Oxford Nanopore Technologies (ONT) sequencing may improve antiretroviral resistance profiling by allowing for long-read clustering. A new ONT sequencing-based method for profiling DRMs in HIV quasispecies was developed and validated. The ONT results were compared to those obtained with Sanger sequencing and Illumina sequencing in 77 HIV-positive plasma samples to evaluate the diagnostic performance. 
For nanopore sequencing, libraries were constructed with SQK-LSK109, EXP-NBD104, and EXP-NBD114, following the official protocols of Native Barcoding Amplicons. At most 12 libraries were pooled and sequenced on ONT GridION for 48 hours using the SUP basecalling mode, with the minimum quality score for read filtering as 10 and the modified demultiplexing setting.
For illumina sequencing, 1 ng of amplicon was used for library preparation with the Nextera XT DNA Library Preparation Kit and IDT® for Illumina® DNA/RNA UD Indexes Set A, Tagmentation. The quality and quantity of the library were assessed with the Bioanalyzer and QIAseq Library Quant Assay Kit, respectively. Libraries were pooled and sequenced with the MiSeq Reagent Kit Nano V2 on the Illumina MiSeq System (250 × 2 cycles).","The paper describes the use of ONT sequencing, Sanger sequencing, and Illumina sequencing methods. It compares the performance of these methods in sequencing the HIV quasispecies."
37537871,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples,"A total of 77 plasma samples, collected from 70 male and 7 female patients ages 18 to 68, were obtained from the Queen Mary Hospital in Hong Kong between 2002 and 2014. An HIV plasmid (pHIV-1_pr-V82A, provided by the European Virus Archive—Global), and 2 clinical samples (Sample ID: KB2061 and KB2979), each of which has a unique quasispecies with a median VAF > 0.9 (Supplemental Table 3), were used to evaluate the clustering performance of ClusterV.",The paper indicates that plasma samples were collected and sequenced to determine the quasispecies and drug resistance mutations.
37537871,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Some,"With the ONT workflow, 4 samples were found harboring different patterns of DRMs in different quasispecies. For example, all of the quasispecies (KB2070_1 and KB0270_2) in the sample KB0270 harbored mutation G73S in the protease gene, as well as mutations M41L, S68G, and M184V in the RT gene, conferring a potentially low-level protease inhibitors resistance (atazanavir, fosamprenavir, indinavir, saquinavir, and nelfinavir) and a low-level to high-level of NRTI resistance (abacavir, didanosine, emtricitabine, and lamivudine). However, mutation T215F was exclusively found in the quasispecies KB0270_2 (abundance = 32.27%), conferring an additional low-intermediate resistance level of NRTI (abacavir, azidothymidine, stavudine, didanosine, and tenofovir).","The paper mentions that some cases were found to have quasispecies with drug resistance mutations (DRMs), which could potentially lead to virological failure."
37537871,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"The research was not a clinical trial, and the patients were not part of one. The study collected samples from patients at a hospital in Hong Kong without mentioning any clinical trial enrollment.

On the development and diagnostic performance evaluation of a new ONT sequencing platform for anti-HIV drug resistance profiling, 77 HIV-positive plasma samples were recruited. These samples were collected from the Queen Mary Hospital in Hong Kong between 2002 and 2014 (Supplemental Table 1).",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial. It describes the collection of samples from patients at a hospital in Hong Kong.
37537871,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Long-Read Sequencing with Hierarchical Clustering for Antiretroviral Resistance Profiling of Mixed Human Immunodeficiency Virus Quasispecies. In this study, 4 out of 59 (6.8%) samples were found to have quasispecies with DRMs. Notably, 2 cases harbored quasispecies with more than one class of DRMs, which could potentially lead to virological failure of first-line ARV therapy. 4 out of 59 (6.8%) samples were found to have quasispecies with discovered distinct patterns of DRMs when applying our ONT workflow, among which 2 harbored quasispecies with more than one class of DRMs.","The paper mentions that some cases were found to have quasispecies with drug resistance mutations (DRMs), which indicates that individuals had previously received ARV drugs."
37537871,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NNRTIs, Protease Inhibitors","Long-Read Sequencing with Hierarchical Clustering for Antiretroviral Resistance Profiling of Mixed Human Immunodeficiency Virus Quasispecies. In this study, 4 out of 59 (6.8%) samples were found to have quasispecies with DRMs. Notably, 2 cases harbored quasispecies with more than one class of DRMs, which could potentially lead to virological failure of first-line ARV therapy. 4 out of 59 (6.8%) samples were found to have quasispecies with discovered distinct patterns of DRMs when applying our ONT workflow, among which 2 harbored quasispecies with more than one class of DRMs.","The paper mentions that some cases were found to have quasispecies with drug resistance mutations (DRMs) to NRTIs, NNRTIs and Protease Inhibitors."
37537871,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Abacavir, Didanosine, Emtricitabine, Lamivudine, Stavudine, Tenofovir, Efavirenz, Nevirapine, Ritonavir, Atazanavir, Saquinavir","with 4 samples harboring distinct patterns of DRMs. For instance, sample KB0270 had all quasispecies (KB2070_1 and KB0270_2) carrying mutation G73S in protease (PR), as well as M41L, S68G, and M184V in reverse transcriptase (RT), indicating possible low-level resistance to PR inhibitors (PIs: atazanavir, saquinavir, ritonavir) plus low to high-level NRTI resistance (abacavir, didanosine, emtricitabine, lamivudine, stavudine, tenofovir). Sample KB2987 had mutation V106I in RT conferring possible low-level NNRTI resistance (efavirenz, nevirapine) in 5 out of 7 quasispecies. Notably, sample KB2987 (7.41%) carried G190E conferring intermediate-high resistance to NNRTI (efavirenz, nevirapine).",The paper provides specific examples of drugs that were effective against viruses that had developed resistance mutations.
