37540331,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"HIV viral load remained undetectable (HIV-RNA < 47 copies/mL) during the 48 weeks of the study in both arms. The absolute CD4 cell count change was not significant between the two groups. The overall proportion of adverse effects in each group was comparable. The rate of adherence to treatment was acceptable in both groups, and no significant difference was observed The triple-drug regimen was changed to dual therapy including TAF 25 mg tablet (Altafir®, Tadbir Kalaye Jam) plus dolutegravir 50 mg tablet (Dolutegravir®, Aurobindo) once daily in the intervention group (TAF plus DTG), and the conventional triple-drug regimens in the control group (3DR). The duration of intervention was 48 weeks for the both groups. A third–party assignment was used for the allocation concealment.","The study does not mention any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure, as it does not focus on sequencing."
