37546367,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,OQ886077 - OQ888150,The partial *pol* nucleotide sequences were submitted to GenBank under the accession numbers: OQ886077 - OQ888150.,The paper provides the specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
37546367,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,2074,A total of 3274 patients were enrolled and 2074 HIV-1 partial *pol* sequences were obtained and subsequently used to establish the dataset.,"The paper states that 2074 HIV-1 partial *pol* sequences were obtained from the 3274 samples collected, indicating that samples from 2074 individuals were used for sequencing."
37546367,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,China,"To monitor the prevalence of HIV-1 drug resistance and to evaluate the risk factors associated with drug resistance in LLVL HIV-1 infections during ART in Guangdong, China. Plasma samples with LLVL during ART in Guangdong Province between Jan 2011 and Dec 2022 were subjected to a modified reverse-transcription PCR with a pre-step of virus concentration by ultracentrifugation before extraction and the Sanger sequencing. Then, the genotypic resistance test was performed and DR was analyzed by the Stanford HIVDB program. Finally, DR-associated factors were identified by logistic regression analysis.","The paper mentions that the samples were collected from patients living in Guangdong, China, which indicates the country of origin for the sequenced samples."
37546367,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2011-2022,"Plasma samples with LLVL during ART in Guangdong Province between Jan 2011 and Dec 2022 were subjected to a modified reverse-transcription PCR with a pre-step of virus concentration by ultracentrifugation before extraction and the Sanger sequencing. A total of 3274 samples were collected from patients living in Guangdong China between Nov 1st, 2011 to Dec 31st, 2022.",The paper specifies that the samples were collected between January 2011 and December 2022.
37546367,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Plasma samples with LLVL during ART in Guangdong Province between Jan 2011 and Dec 2022 were subjected to a modified reverse-transcription PCR with a pre-step of virus concentration by ultracentrifugation before extraction and the Sanger sequencing. Then, the genotypic resistance test was performed and DR was analyzed by the Stanford HIVDB program. Finally, DR-associated factors were identified by logistic regression analysis. Zero point five-milliliter plasma was concentrated by ultracentrifugation at 4°C, 20,000× g for 1 hour. Then, 0.36 mL of the supernatant was removed, and the remaining 0.14 mL was left for nucleic acid extraction. RNA was extracted from the concentrated sample using the QIAamp Viral RNA Mini Kit (Qiagen, German). The partial HIV-1 pol gene (HXB2 nt 2253–3252) was amplified by one-step RT-PCR and nested PCR as previously described.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes the use of direct sequencing methods.
37546367,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,pol,"The partial HIV-1 *pol* gene (HXB2 nt 2253--3252) was amplified by one-step RT-PCR and nested PCR as previously described. Finally, partial *pol* sequences were obtained from 2074 out of 3274 samples (63.35%) in this analysis.",The paper specifies that the partial *pol* gene was sequenced from the clinical samples.
37546367,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"Plasma samples with LLVL during ART in Guangdong Province between Jan 2011 and Dec 2022 were subjected to a modified reverse-transcription PCR with a pre-step of virus concentration by ultracentrifugation before extraction and the Sanger sequencing. Then, the genotypic resistance test was performed and DR was analyzed by the Stanford HIVDB program. Finally, DR-associated factors were identified by logistic regression analysis.",The paper explicitly states that Sanger sequencing was used for sequencing the HIV-1 pol gene.
37546367,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"Plasma samples with LLVL during ART in Guangdong Province between Jan 2011 and Dec 2022 were subjected to a modified reverse-transcription PCR with a pre-step of virus concentration by ultracentrifugation before extraction and the Sanger sequencing. Then, the genotypic resistance test was performed and DR was analyzed by the Stanford HIVDB program. Finally, DR-associated factors were identified by logistic regression analysis. Zero point five-milliliter plasma was concentrated by ultracentrifugation at 4°C, 20,000× g for 1 hour. Then, 0.36 mL of the supernatant was removed, and the remaining 0.14 mL was left for nucleic acid extraction. RNA was extracted from the concentrated sample using the QIAamp Viral RNA Mini Kit (Qiagen, German).",The paper mentions that plasma samples were collected and used for sequencing.
37546367,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"HIV-1 infected individuals were eligible for inclusion in this study if they have received ART for at least 6 months with HIV-1 viral load between 200 to 1000 copies/mL. To monitor the prevalence of HIV-1 drug resistance and to evaluate the risk factors associated with drug resistance in LLVL HIV-1 infections during ART in Guangdong, China.","The paper mentions that the study focused on patients with low-level viremia (200-1000 copies/mL) after at least 6 months of ART, which indicates the sequences were obtained from patients with virological failure."
37546367,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"HIV-1 infected individuals were eligible for inclusion in this study if they have received ART for at least 6 months with HIV-1 viral load between 200 to 1000 copies/mL. A total of 3274 samples were collected from patients living in Guangdong China between Nov 1st, 2011 to Dec 31st, 2022",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial; it describes a retrospective study of clinical samples.
37546367,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,HIV-1 infected individuals were eligible for inclusion in this study if they have received ART for at least 6 months with HIV-1 viral load between 200 to 1000 copies/mL. Plasma samples with LLVL during ART in Guangdong Province between Jan 2011 and Dec 2022 were subjected to a modified reverse-transcription PCR with a pre-step of virus concentration by ultracentrifugation before extraction and the Sanger sequencing.,"The paper mentions that the study included patients who had received antiretroviral therapy (ART) for at least 6 months, indicating that the sequences were obtained from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
37546367,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI","The Stanford HIV dbprogram 9.4 (last updated on 7th Dec. 2022, ) was used to identify DRMs and infer resistance to antiretroviral drugs, including protease inhibitors (PI), nucleoside reverse- transcriptase inhibitors (NRTI) and non-nucleoside reverse-transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTI).","The paper mentions the mutations associated with drug resistance to protease inhibitors (PIs), nucleoside reverse-transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs), and non-nucleoside reverse-transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs), indicating that individuals had received these drug classes before sequencing."
37546367,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"AZT, ABC, FTC, 3TC, TDF, D4T, DDI, NVP, EFV, ETR, RPV, DOR","The HIV-1 resistance levels and percentage of 20 ARV drugs were analyzed, as shown in Figure 3. For NRTI, the resistance to seven NRTI ranged from 6.12% (127/2074) to 33.27% (690/2074). DR to AZT (6.12%) was significantly lower than that to ABC (33.27%) (χ2=457.008, p<0.001), FTC (32.88%) (χ2=447.724, p<0.001), 3TC (32.88%) (χ2=447.724, p<0.001), TDF (14.75%) (χ2=80.438, p<0.001), D4T (17.60%) (χ2=126.652, p<0.001) and DDI (20.06%) (χ2=170.982, p<0.001) ( Figure 3B ). For NNRTI, the resistance to five NNRTI ranged from 19.19% (398/2074) to 40.07% (831/2074), and the DR prevalence to NVP and EFV was 40.07% (831/2074) and 39.68% (823/2074), respectively. ETR (19.19%) showed the lowest DR frequency, followed by RPV (24.73%), DOR (24.78%), EFV (39.68%), and NVP (40.07%) (χ2=331.422, p<0.001).","The paper lists specific drugs under each class for which resistance was analyzed, indicating that individuals had received these drugs before sequencing."
