37573167,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,We aimed at evaluating the temporal trend of drug-resistance and APOBEC editing from HIV-DNA genotypic resistance tests (GRT) in virologically suppressed individuals. HIV-1 DNA was obtained from whole-blood (N=180) or lymphomonocytic cells (N=936) after separation from peripheral blood from HIV-1-infected patients with a Ficoll-Hypaque gradient.,"The paper mentions the collection of HIV-1 DNA from patient samples, indicating that sequences were obtained from these samples."
