37573167,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"Protease, Reverse Transcriptase, Integrase",A sequence was considered affected by APOBEC editing when at least one APOBEC related mutation (APO-M) or a stop codon (APO-stop) was detected in protease/reverse transcriptase (PR/RT) or integrase. The presence of the 18 APOBEC context drug resistance mutations (APO-DRM) according to Stanford HIVdb algorithm was also evaluated.,"The paper mentions the detection of mutations in the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes."
