37573167,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,The presence of MRM in HIV-DNA GRT performed on triple therapy experienced individuals in the context of a treatment history of 7 Regimens for 1.7 Virologically Supressed. Maraviroc; Raltegravir; Etravirine; Tenofovir; Emtricitabine; Abacavir; Atazanavir; Lopinavir; Raltegravir; Atazanavir. CD4 T-lymphocytes HIV-DNA was obtained from HIV-1 infected patients. This retrospective study included 1126 HIV-1 drug-experienced virologically suppressed subjects with an available HIV-DNA GRT over the period 2010-2021 performed for routine clinical practice in several reference centers in Italy.,The paper mentions the presence of MRM in HIV-DNA GRT performed on triple therapy experienced individuals.
37573167,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI, INSTI, CCR5 antagonist","The presence of MRM in HIV-DNA GRT performed on triple therapy experienced individuals in the context of a treatment history of 7 Regimens for 1.7 Virologically Supressed. Maraviroc; Raltegravir; Etravirine; Tenofovir; Emtricitabine; Abacavir; Atazanavir; Lopinavir; Raltegravir; Atazanavir. Lopinavir/ritonavir - PI (protease antagonists); Saquinavir - PI. Tenofovir DF or d4T or abacavir or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate - NRTI (nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors); Emtricitabine or lamivudine - NRTI; Zidovudine - NRTI Emtricitabine or lamivudine; Atripla - NNRTI (Non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors); Etravirine; Rilpivirine - NNRTI; Raltegravir or dolutegravir - INI (integrase inhibitors); Etravirine - Fuzeon enfuvirtide - FI (fusion inhibitors) - Raltegravir - INSTI (integrase inhibitors); Maraviroc - CCR5 antagonist (entry inhibitor). Total of 43 regimens had an NRTI backbone. Of 1126 individuals, 11.6% had previously received a Maraviroc, 15.3% an INST, 31.5% a PI, or 41.2% an ETR or RIL based regimens.",The paper lists various antiretroviral drugs from different classes that were included in the treatment regimens of the individuals included in the study.
37573167,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Tenofovir DF, d4T, abacavir, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, Emtricitabine, lamivudine, Zidovudine, maraviroc, Rilpivirine, Etravirine, Raltegravir, Dolutegravir, Lopinavir, Raltegravir, atazanavir, Saquinavir, Etravirine, rilpivirine, Raltegravir, Raltegravir, Maraviroc, Etravirine, Tenofovir DF, Atripla","The presence of MRM in HIV-DNA GRT performed on triple therapy experienced individuals in the context of a treatment history of 7 Regimens for 1.7 Virologically Supressed. Maraviroc; Raltegravir; Etravirine; Tenofovir; Emtricitabine; Abacavir; Atazanavir; Lopinavir; Raltegravir; Atazanavir. Lopinavir/ritonavir - PI (protease antagonists); Saquinavir - PI. Tenofovir DF or d4T or abacavir or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate - NRTI (nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors); Emtricitabine or lamivudine - NRTI; Zidovudine - NRTI Emtricitabine or lamivudine; Atripla - NNRTI (Non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors); Etravirine; Rilpivirine - NNRTI; Raltegravir or dolutegravir - INI (integrase inhibitors); Etravirine - Fuzeon enfuvirtide - FI (fusion inhibitors) - Raltegravir - INSTI (integrase inhibitors); Maraviroc - CCR5 antagonist (entry inhibitor) . Persons having sustained virological suppression for more than three year achieved it with a median of 3 either NRTI-based regimens (1.0), with or without enfuvirtide (42.9%) or maraviroc (18.6%) associated within ETR-based (39.4%), RPV-based (28.6%), INI-based (22.4%), PI/r-based (16.4%), or RAL-based regimens (15.8%). Of the 620 individuals having 2 NRTI-based: 620 (55.0%) had previously received 2 NRTI-based regimens, 116 (10.31%) an ETR-based, 78 (6.93%) an RPV-based, HIV-1 DNA was obtained from whole-blood or lymphomonocytic cells after separation from peripheral blood from HIV-1-infected patients with a Ficoll-Hypaque gradient, as described previously. HIV-1 DNA was extracted from PBMCs by using a commercially available kit (QIAampDNAViral minikit).",The paper lists various antiretroviral drugs from different classes that were included in the treatment regimens of the individuals included in the study.
