ore sample sequencing.
37674678,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"HIV-1 pol gene sequence was obtained by viral RNA extraction and nested PCR amplification; A total of 1,161 sequences were successfully sequenced, of which CRF07_BC (40.6%), CRF01_AE (38.4%) and CRF105_0107 (6.3%) were the main HIV-1 genotypes.","The paper explicitly states that HIV-1 pol gene sequences were obtained from plasma samples of 1,393 newly diagnosed HIV-1 infected individuals. It mentions that these samples were collected between January 2019 and December 2021 in Nanjing, China, and provides details on the sequencing methods used, indicating that the sequences were derived from patient samples."
37674678,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The degree of drug resistance to each ART drug was divided into five levels: susceptible (S, 0--9), potential low resistance (PLR, 10--14), low-level resistance (LR, 15--29), intermediate-level resistance (IR, 30--59), and high-level resistance categories (HR, ≥60).",The paper discusses drug resistance mutations and their prevalence but does not mention any in vitro susceptibility testing or data related to the effectiveness of specific drugs against the virus in a laboratory setting.
37674678,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"The authors acknowledge that the data presented in this study must be deposited and made publicly available in an acceptable repository, prior to publication. Frontiers cannot accept a manuscript that does not adhere to our open data policies.","The paper mentions that the data must be deposited in a publicly acceptable repository, indicating that they have not yet been made publicly available."
