37674678,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,China,"Transmitted drug resistance and transmission clusters among ART-naïve HIV-1-infected individuals from 2019 to 2021 in Nanjing, China Our study revealed that the major HIV-1 genotypes detected in Nanjing were CRF07_BC, CRF01_AE and CRF105_01B.","The paper specifies that the study was conducted in Nanjing, China, and all samples were collected from this location."
37674678,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2019 to 2021,"A total of 1,393 participants who were newly diagnosed with HIV-1 and had not received ART between January 2019 and December 2021 were enrolled in this study.","The paper mentions that participants were enrolled between January 2019 and December 2021, indicating the timeframe during which the samples were obtained."
37674678,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"RNA extraction, nested-PCR, and sequencing of viral DNA Within 12 h after blood collection, plasma was isolated and kept at −80°C until analysis. Viral RNA was extracted from 200 μl plasma samples using the QIAamp Viral RNA Mini Kit (Qiagen, Hilden, Germany). The target fragment of 1,059 bp in the pol gene (HXB2:2253--3,312) was amplified using nested polymerase chain reaction (PCR).","The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes the use of nested PCR and direct sequencing of the PCR products, which indicates that cloning was not a part of the methodology."
37674678,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,HIV-1 pol gene,"The target fragment of 1,059 bp in the pol gene (HXB2:2253--3,312) was amplified using nested polymerase chain reaction (PCR).","The paper specifies that the HIV-1 pol gene was sequenced, and it provides details on the region of the pol gene that was targeted for amplification and sequencing."
