37878637,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"TDF, 3TC, EFV","Most of the participants (34.5%, 31.3%, and 31.7%) were on a TDF + 3TC + EFV-based regimen (Table 2).","The paper provides specific details about the antiretroviral regimens of the participants, mentioning that the majority were on a TDF + 3TC + EFV-based regimen."
37880705,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics.,"The paper mentions that HIV-1 pol sequences were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed, indicating that HIV sequences from patient samples were reported."
37880705,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Abstract; Background; Ethiopia is among the highly HIV-affected countries, with reported 12,000 and 12,000 AIDS-related deaths and incidents as per reports from 2021. Although the country has made a promising progress in antiretroviral therapy, recent studies have indicated that pretreatment drug resistance (PDR) is alarmingly increasing, which has become a challenge for the effectiveness of HIV treatment. Epidemiologic data on PDR is necessary to help establish ART regimens with good efficacy. Thus, this systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia.","The paper focuses on pretreatment drug resistance (PDR) and HIV-1 variant dynamics among ART-naïve individuals, and does not mention in vitro drug susceptibility testing or data."
37880705,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,"Sequences of the included studies were downloaded from GenBank if they were publicly available and, if they were not found online, study authors were contacted for the respective sequences","The paper mentions that sequences were retrieved from GenBank, which indicates that they were made publicly available."
37880705,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,"We identified nine studies and analyzed 1070 retrieved HIV-1 pol sequences in this systematic review. The pooled prevalence of PDR was 4.8% (51/1070), including 1.4% (15/1070), 2.8% (30/1070), and 0.8% (9/1070) for nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI), non-NRTI (NNRTI), and protease inhibitor (PI) resistance, respectively",The paper does not mention the specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
37880705,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,1070,"We identified nine studies and analyzed 1070 retrieved HIV-1 pol sequences in this systematic review. Sequences of the included studies were downloaded from GenBank if they were publicly available and, if they were not found online, study authors were contacted for the respective sequences","The paper states that 1070 HIV-1 pol sequences were analyzed in this systematic review, indicating that samples were obtained from 1070 individuals."
37880705,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Ethiopia,This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics.,"The paper focuses on HIV-1 sequences from ART-naïve individuals in Ethiopia, indicating that the samples were obtained from this country."
37880705,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2003 to 2018,HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics.,"The paper mentions that the studies from which the sequences were retrieved were conducted between 2003 and 2018, indicating the years from which the samples were obtained."
37880705,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"The online databases Google Scholar and PubMed were searched for PDR in Ethiopia to identify relevant literature published until March 30, 2023. The search for the literature was done using the following search terms: [“human immunodeficiency virus” OR HIV OR AIDS OR “acquired immunodeficiency syndrome”] AND [“antiretroviral therapy” OR HAART OR ART] AND [“drug resistance” OR naïve OR “pregnant women” OR antenatal OR subtype OR surveillance] AND (Ethiopia). In addition, the International AIDS Society (IAS) Conference, and Conference on Retroviruses and Opportunistic Infections (CROI) databases were also searched for additional articles. Upon duplicate removal, all retrieved publications were reviewed to determine which studies contained data regarding PDR in Ethiopia. All PDR studies that involved ART-naïve HIV-infected individuals aged ≥ 14 years old in Ethiopia were included in this review. We excluded studies conducted in children, those that have incomplete sequences (did not contain complete PR (99 codons) and partial RT (the first 230 codons), and those studies that were done among ART-experienced individuals (Fig. 1 ).",The paper does not mention any use of cloning samples prior to sequencing. Samples from other studies were directly analyzed.
37880705,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,HIV-1 protease and partial reverse transcriptase (RT),"This paper the analyzed sequences (from the total of 1226 retrieved sequences) that have full protease and partial RT. We identified nine studies and analyzed 1070 retrieved HIV-1 pol sequences in this systematic review. According to this systematic review, the overall pooled prevalence of PDR is low.","The paper mentions that the protease and partial RT regions were sequenced. and analyzed, indicating that these genes were reported to have been sequenced."
37880705,10,What method was used for sequencing?,The paper does not specify the sequencing method used.,This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics.,"The paper does not mention the specific sequencing method used, as it focuses on the analysis of sequences retrieved from other studies."
37880705,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,The paper does not specify the type of clinical specimens sequenced.,This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics.,"The paper does not specify the type of clinical specimens sequenced, as it focuses on the analysis of sequences retrieved from other studies."
37880705,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. HIV-1 pol sequences from studies conducted between 2003 and 2018 among ART-naïve Ethiopian individuals were retrieved from GenBank and analyzed for the presence of PDR mutations (PDRM) along with the analysis of HIV-1 variant dynamics.,"The paper mentions that the study focused on ART-naïve individuals, which means sequences from individuals with virological failure were not obtained."
37880705,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"All PDR studies that involved ART-naïve HIV-infected individuals aged ≥ 14 years old in Ethiopia were included in this review. We excluded studies conducted in children, those that have incomplete sequences (did not contain complete PR (99 codons) and partial RT (the first 230 codons), and those studies that were done among ART-experienced individuals.",The paper does not mention whether the patients were part of a clinical trial; it focused on a systematic review of existing studies.
37880705,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. All PDR studies that involved ART-naïve HIV-infected individuals aged ≥ 14 years old in Ethiopia were included in this review. We excluded studies conducted in children, those that have incomplete sequences (did not contain complete PR (99 codons) and partial RT (the first 230 codons), and those studies that were done among ART-experienced individuals.","The paper mentions that the study focused on ART-naïve individuals, indicating that sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs were not reported."
37880705,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,The paper does not report any drug classes received by individuals before sample sequencing.,"This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. All PDR studies that involved ART-naïve HIV-infected individuals aged ≥ 14 years old in Ethiopia were included in this review. We excluded studies conducted in children, those that have incomplete sequences (did not contain complete PR (99 codons) and partial RT (the first 230 codons), and those studies that were done among ART-experienced individuals.","Paper focused on ART-naïve individuals, not reporting drug classes received before sequencing."
37880705,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,The paper does not report any drugs received by individuals before sample sequencing.,"This systematic review aimed to determine the trend analysis of PDR among ART-naïve individuals along with HIV variant dynamics in Ethiopia. All PDR studies that involved ART-naïve HIV-infected individuals aged ≥ 14 years old in Ethiopia were included in this review. We excluded studies conducted in children, those that have incomplete sequences (did not contain complete PR (99 codons) and partial RT (the first 230 codons), and those studies that were done among ART-experienced individuals.","Paper focused on ART-naïve individuals, not reporting drugs received before sequencing."
37896785,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,The nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank.,The paper reports the results of genetic studies on HIV-1 samples obtained from pregnant women in Ho Chi Minh City. It specifically mentions that the nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained.
37896785,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The aim of our work was to analyze subtypic structure and drug-resistant variants of HIV in pregnant women in Ho Chi Minh City. The study material was blood plasma samples from HIV-infected pregnant women: 31 women showed virological failure of ART, and 30 women had not previously received therapy. HIV-1 genotyping and mutation detection were performed based on analysis of the nucleotide sequences of the pol gene region.",The paper focuses on genetic sequencing and the presence of drug resistance mutations in HIV-1 samples from pregnant women. It does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing or results.
37896785,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,The nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank (numbers OQ215322-OQ215382).,"The paper explicitly states that the nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank, indicating that the sequences were made publicly available."
37896785,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,OQ215322-OQ215382,The nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank (numbers OQ215322-OQ215382).,"The paper provides the specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, listing them as OQ215322 to OQ215382."
37896785,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,61,The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma.,The paper mentions that the study included blood plasma samples from 61 pregnant women.
37896785,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Vietnam,The aim of our work was to analyze subtypic structure and drug-resistant variants of HIV in pregnant women in Ho Chi Minh City. The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma.,"The study was conducted in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam, and the samples were collected from pregnant women in this city."
37896785,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2021,The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma.,The paper specifies that the blood plasma samples were collected in 2021.
37896785,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"For samples with a detectable viral load, reverse transcription and PCR were performed, followed by Sanger sequencing using the AmpliSens HIVResist-Seq (Central Research Institute of Epidemiology, Moscow, Russia) commercial kit. The nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank (numbers OQ215322-OQ215382).","The paper describes direct sequencing of the PCR products, indicating that samples were not cloned prior to sequencing."
37896785,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,pol gene region (protease and part of reverse transcriptase),HIV-1 genotyping and mutation detection were performed based on analysis of the nucleotide sequences of the pol gene region. The nucleotide sequences of 61 HIV-1 samples were obtained and deposited in GenBank (numbers OQ215322-OQ215382).,"The paper mentions that HIV-1 genotyping was performed based on the analysis of the nucleotide sequences of the *pol* gene region, which includes protease (PR) and part of reverse transcriptase (RT)."
37896785,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"For samples with a detectable viral load, reverse transcription and PCR were performed, followed by Sanger sequencing using the AmpliSens HIVResist-Seq (Central Research Institute of Epidemiology, Moscow, Russia) commercial kit.",The paper describes the use of Sanger sequencing for analyzing the HIV-1 samples.
37896785,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Blood plasma,The study material was blood plasma samples from HIV-infected pregnant women. The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma.,The paper specifies that blood plasma samples from HIV-infected pregnant women were used for sequencing.
37896785,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"In the surveyed group, 31 women showed virological failure of ART, and 30 women had not previously received therapy. NRTI mutations were present only in women with virological failure of ART.","The paper mentions that 31 women in the study showed virological failure of ART, and their samples were used for sequencing."
37896785,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,The study material was blood plasma samples collected in 2021 from 61 pregnant women in need of PMTCT in Ho Chi Minh City with a viral load above 500 copies per ml of blood plasma.,The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial; they were pregnant women in need of PMTCT.
37896785,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"In the surveyed group, 31 women showed virological failure of ART, and 30 women had not previously received therapy. HIV-infected pregnant women should undergo monthly monitoring, especially before the expected date of delivery.","The paper reports that 31 women in the study showed virological failure of ART, indicating they had previously received ARV drugs."
37896785,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NRTI, PI-NNRTI","We previously reported that the number of naturally occurring polymorphs in the protease region among ART users ranged from 17 to 35 mutations and also depended on the number of ART regimens. In the present study, polymorphic mutations were found to be fewer, most likely due to the lack of ART or the single therapy regimen that women received.","The paper mentions that women with virological failure had received various ART regimens, including NRTIs and PIs."
37896785,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"lamivudine (3TC), stavudine (d4T), zidovudine (AZT), nevirapine (NVP), efavirenz (EFV)","In Vietnam, available three-drug first-line ART regimens meet WHO standards: two NRTIs (stavudine (d4T)/lamivudine (3TC) or zidovudine (AZT)/lamivudine) together with one NNRTI (nevirapine (NVP) or efavirenz (EFV)). Our previously published study on women with virologically ineffective ART in Ho Chi Minh City showed a high prevalence of HIV drug resistance mutations. We previously reported that the number of naturally occurring polymorphs in the protease region among ART users ranged from 17 to 35 mutations and also depended on the number of ART regimens.","The paper lists specific NRTIs and NNRTIs that were part of the available first-line therapy regimens in Vietnam, and mentions that women with virologically ineffective ART were included in the study."
37896860,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"""DRT requests for 106 (15%) children across the two study groups; HIV drug resistance patterns and characteristics associated with clinically significant drug resistance among children with virologic failure on antiretroviral treatment in Kenya; DRT detected mutations associated with DR in all participants tested, with 93 (88%) having major mutations, including 51 (54%) with dual-class resistance; DR is highly prevalent among CHIV on ART with VF in Kenya.""","The paper discusses drug resistance testing (DRT) conducted on plasma samples from children with HIV on antiretroviral treatment in Kenya. It mentions that DRT detected mutations associated with drug resistance in all participants tested, indicating that HIV sequences from patient samples were analyzed."
37896860,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"HIV Drug Resistance Patterns and Characteristics Associated with Clinically Significant Drug Resistance among Children with Virologic Failure on Antiretroviral Treatment in Kenya: Findings from the Opt4Kids Randomized Controlled Trial; Drug resistance (DR) is highly prevalent among CHIV on ART with VF in Kenya. We describe DR mutations and present logistic regression models to identify factors associated with clinically significant DR. We enrolled 704 children in the study; the median age was 9 years (interquartile range (IQR) 7, 12), 344 (49%) were female, and the median time on ART was 5 years (IQR 3, 8). During the study period, 106 (15%) children had DRT results (84 intervention and 22 control).",The paper focuses on drug resistance testing and the genetic mutations associated with drug resistance in HIV samples from children. It does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility assays or results.
37896860,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,The de-identified data presented in this study are available on request from the corresponding author. The data are not publicly available due to the sensitive nature of the disease being studied.,The paper states that the de-identified data are available on request from the corresponding author but does not mention that the sequences are publicly available.
37896860,4,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not provided,"Abstract. Drug Resistance Testing (DRT) for HIV: CHIV with Virologic Failure on ART in Kenya. We describe DR mutations and present logistic regression models to identify factors associated with clinically significant DR. We enrolled 704 children in the study; the median age was 9 years (interquartile range (IQR) 7, 12), 344 (49%) were female, and the median time on ART was 5 years (IQR 3, 8). During the study period, 106 (15%) children had DRT results (84 intervention and 22 control). The DRT result reports contained a list of the DR genotypes as well as phenotypic interpretations. Here, we report DRT-M genotypic results; house- and INSTI-R testing were not performed.","The paper does not provide any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates. This information is typically included in the methods or results sections, but it is absent in this case."
37896860,5,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,704,We enrolled 704 children in the study; HIV Drug Resistance Patterns and Characteristics Associated with Clinically Significant Drug Resistance among Children with Virologic Failure on Antiretroviral Treatment in Kenya: Findings from the Opt4Kids Randomized Controlled Trial,"The paper states that a total of 704 children were enrolled in the study, and samples were obtained for drug resistance testing, indicating that this is the number of individuals from whom samples were obtained for HIV sequencing."
37896860,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Kenya,"""Increasing HIV drug resistance (DR) among children with HIV (CHIV) on antiretroviral treatment (ART) is concerning. CHIV ages 1--14 years enrolled from March 2019 to December 2020 from five facilities in Kisumu County, Kenya, were included. We describe DR mutations and present logistic regression models to identify factors associated with clinically significant DR. We enrolled 704 children in the study; the median age was 9 years (interquartile range (IQR) 7, 12), 344 (49%) were female, and the median time on ART was 5 years (IQR 3, 8)"" HIV Drug Resistance Patterns and Characteristics Associated with Clinically Significant Drug Resistance among Children with Virologic Failure on Antiretroviral Treatment in Kenya: Findings from the Opt4Kids Randomized Controlled Trial","The paper describes a study conducted in Kenya, specifically Kisumu County, where children with HIV were enrolled and samples were collected for drug resistance testing."
37896860,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2019-2020,"Children were randomized 1:1 to control (standard-of-care) or intervention (point-of-care viral load (POC VL) testing every three months with targeted genotypic drug resistance testing (DRT) for virologic failure (VF) (≥1000 copies/mL)). CHIV ages 1–14 years enrolled from March 2019 to December 2020 from five facilities in Kisumu County, Kenya, were included. In brief, 704 CHIV ages 1–14 years were enrolled from 5 public facilities in Kisumu County, Kenya, between March and December 2019 and were followed for 12 months. The Optimizing Viral Suppression in Children on ART in Kenya (Opt4Kids) study protocol and primary findings have been described previously. Of note, 536 (76%) were virally suppressed, 77 (11%) had VF, 91 (13%) had missing VL data, and 20 participants newly initiated ART within 30 days of study enrollment.","The paper states that children were enrolled in the study from March 2019 to December 2020, and samples were collected during this period for drug resistance testing."
37896860,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"HIV drug resistance testing was performed on plasma samples using Sanger sequencing with Applied Biosystems 3130xl Genetic Analyzers (ThermoFisher Scientific, Nairobi, Kenya) at the KEMRI-CDC HIV Research and Sanger 3730xl at the Kenya National HIV Reference Laboratories. These laboratories utilize validated, WHO-certified, optimized in-house assays to detect reverse transcriptase and PI mutations. Integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI) mutations were not routinely evaluated during the study period. The DRT result reports contained a list of the DR genotypes as well as phenotypic interpretations based on the scoring systems generated by the Stanford Genotypic Resistance Interpretation Algorithm (Stanford Univeristy, Palo Alto, CA, USA) versions available during the study period.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It focuses on drug resistance testing using Sanger sequencing without any mention of cloning procedures.
37896860,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"RT, PR","HIV drug resistance testing was performed on plasma samples using Sanger sequencing with Applied Biosystems 3130xl Genetic Analyzers (ThermoFisher Scientific, Nairobi, Kenya) at the KEMRI-CDC HIV Research and Sanger 3730xl at the Kenya National HIV Reference Laboratories. These laboratories utilize validated, WHO-certified, optimized in-house assays to detect reverse transcriptase and PI mutations. Integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI) mutations were not routinely evaluated during the study period. The DRT result reports contained a list of the DR genotypes as well as phenotypic interpretations based on the scoring systems generated by the Stanford Genotypic Resistance Interpretation Algorithm (Stanford Univeristy, Palo Alto, CA, USA) versions available during the study period.","The paper mentions that drug resistance testing was performed to detect reverse transcriptase and protease mutations, indicating that these genes were sequenced."
37896860,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"HIV drug resistance testing was performed on plasma samples using Sanger sequencing with Applied Biosystems 3130xl Genetic Analyzers (ThermoFisher Scientific, Nairobi, Kenya) at the KEMRI-CDC HIV Research and Sanger 3730xl at the Kenya National HIV Reference Laboratories. These laboratories utilize validated, WHO-certified, optimized in-house assays to detect reverse transcriptase and PI mutations. Integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI) mutations were not routinely evaluated during the study period. The DRT result reports contained a list of the DR genotypes as well as phenotypic interpretations based on the scoring systems generated by the Stanford Genotypic Resistance Interpretation Algorithm (Stanford Univeristy, Palo Alto, CA, USA) versions available during the study period.",The paper explicitly states that drug resistance testing was performed using Sanger sequencing with Applied Biosystems 3130xl Genetic Analyzers.
37896860,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"HIV drug resistance testing was performed on plasma samples using Sanger sequencing with Applied Biosystems 3130xl Genetic Analyzers (ThermoFisher Scientific, Nairobi, Kenya) at the KEMRI-CDC HIV Research and Sanger 3730xl at the Kenya National HIV Reference Laboratories. These laboratories utilize validated, WHO-certified, optimized in-house assays to detect reverse transcriptase and PI mutations. Integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI) mutations were not routinely evaluated during the study period. The DRT result reports contained a list of the DR genotypes as well as phenotypic interpretations based on the scoring systems generated by the Stanford Genotypic Resistance Interpretation Algorithm (Stanford Univeristy, Palo Alto, CA, USA) versions available during the study period.",The paper mentions that HIV drug resistance testing was performed on plasma samples obtained from study participants.
37896860,12,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"""Increasing HIV drug resistance (DR) among children with HIV (CHIV) on antiretroviral treatment (ART) is concerning. Drug resistance (DR) is highly prevalent among CHIV on ART with VF in Kenya. We enrolled 704 children in the study; the median age was 9 years (interquartile range (IQR) 7, 12), 344 (49%) were female, and the median time on ART was 5 years (IQR 3, 8). During the study period, 106 (15%) children had DRT results (84 intervention and 22 control). We describe DR mutations and present logistic regression models to identify factors associated with clinically significant DR. We enrolled 704 children in the study; the median age was 9 years (interquartile range (IQR) 7, 12), 344 (49%) were female, and the median time on ART was 5 years (IQR 3, 8). During the study period, 106 (15%) children had DRT results (84 intervention and 22 control)."" HIV Drug Resistance Patterns and Characteristics Associated with Clinically Significant Drug Resistance among Children with Virologic Failure on Antiretroviral Treatment in Kenya: Findings from the Opt4Kids Randomized Controlled Trial; Virologic failure (VF) was defined as any VL result ≥ 1000 copies/mL.","The paper specifically mentions that drug resistance testing was conducted for children with virologic failure on antiretroviral treatment, indicating that sequences were obtained from these individuals."
37896860,13,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"""Increasing HIV drug resistance (DR) among children with HIV (CHIV) on antiretroviral treatment (ART) is concerning. Drug resistance (DR) is highly prevalent among CHIV on ART with VF in Kenya. We enrolled 704 children in the study; the median age was 9 years (interquartile range (IQR) 7, 12), 344 (49%) were female, and the median time on ART was 5 years (IQR 3, 8). During the study period, 106 (15%) children had DRT results (84 intervention and 22 control). We describe DR mutations and present logistic regression models to identify factors associated with clinically significant DR. We enrolled 704 children in the study; the median age was 9 years (interquartile range (IQR) 7, 12), 344 (49%) were female, and the median time on ART was 5 years (IQR 3, 8). During the study period, 106 (15%) children had DRT results (84 intervention and 22 control). Children were individually randomized 1:1, stratified by site and age groups (ages 1–9 years and 10–14 years), to the control (standard-of-care) or intervention groups (point-of-care viral load testing every three months with DRT for those with VF (HIV RNA ≥ 1000 copies/mL)) and followed for 12 months."". The Optimizing Viral Suppression in Children on ART in Kenya (Opt4Kids) study protocol and primary findings have been described previously. In brief, 704 CHIV ages 1–14 years were enrolled from 5 public facilities in Kisumu County, Kenya, between March and December 2019 and were followed for 12 months.","The paper is based on findings from the Opt4Kids randomized controlled trial, which indicates that the patients were part of a clinical trial."
37896860,14,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Children were randomly assigned to control (standard-of-care) or intervention (point-of-care viral load (POC VL) testing every three months with targeted genotypic drug resistance testing (DRT) for virologic failure (VF) (≥1000 copies/mL)). Of note, 536 (76%) were virally suppressed, 77 (11%) had VF, 91 (13%) had missing VL data, and 20 participants newly initiated ART within 30 days of study enrollment. We abstracted routinely collected data from standardized Ministry of Health forms in medical files and registers using direct, electronic data entry via tablets into a REDCap database. Similarly, we entered study-collected data, including DRT results, in this REDCap database.","The paper mentions that children with HIV on antiretroviral treatment were enrolled in the study, indicating that sequences were obtained from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs."
37896860,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI","A total of 382/704 (54.3%) of participants were on an NNRTI-containing regimen at study enrollment, 294 (41.8%) were on a PI-containing regimen, and 27 (3.8%) were on an INSTI-containing regimen; The DRT result reports contained a list of the DR genotypes as well as phenotypic interpretations based on the scoring systems generated by the Stanford Genotypic Resistance Interpretation Algorithm (Stanford Univeristy, Palo Alto, CA, USA) versions available during the study period. Integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI) mutations were not routinely evaluated during the study period.","The paper mentions that the children were on NNRTI, NRTI or PI-based regimens during the study. The study included DRT for participants on INSTIs but evaluated RT and PI genes only."
37896860,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Abacavir, lamivudine, zidovudine, lopinavir, ritonavir, efavirenz, dolutegravir","First-line ART regimens in Kenya during the study period for children included lamivudine with either abacavir (preferred) or zidovudine (alternative) and lopinavir/ritonavir for those less than three years of age and lamivudine with either abacavir (preferred) or zidovudine (alternative) and efavirenz for those three years of age and older. Second-line ART regimens included changes in NRTI medication from abacavir to zidovudine or vice versa depending on which the child was on as first-line with maintenance of lamivudine. Those on lopinavir/ritonavir as first-line required review by the HIV Technical Working Group to recommend a second-line regimen, while those on efavirenz were recommended to switch to lopinavir/ritonavir. In 2020, the guidelines were updated to recommend dolutegravir (DTG) for those weighing at least 20 kg for treatment initiation and optimization (switch to DTG-containing regimen regardless of viral load), which was rolled out during the study period.","The paper mentions that children were on various ART regimens that included drugs like lamivudine, abacavir, zidovudine, lopinavir, ritonavir and efavirenz and dolutegravir."
