37920909,7,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2020 to 2023,"The current study recruited 629 ART-naïve individuals from Tianjin Second People’s Hospital between January 1, 2020, and April 1, 2023.","The paper specifies that the samples were collected between January 1, 2020, and April 1, 2023."
37920909,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,no,"After RNA extraction, an in-house genotyping method and standard Sanger sequencing were used to amplify and sequence HIV-1 integrase genes, as described previously. HIV-1 subtypes were determined using the REGA HIV-1 Subtyping Tool (version 3.0, https://www.genomedetective.com/app/typingtool/hiv). We used the Stanford University HIV Drug Resistance Database (HIVDB Algorithm version 9.4.1) to examine mutations. Sequences with resistance levels classified as low, intermediate, and high were all regarded as resistant.","The paper describes the use of standard Sanger sequencing, which is not compatible with clone sequencing."
