37938856,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"In the intervention group, from enrolment up until 6 months postpartum, we identified 54 episodes of VL>1000 copies/ml, among 48 (11.7%) participants (Table 3). In the intervention group, 52 DRM tests were requested, of which 46 (88%) were successfully conducted (six samples failed to amplify) and all identified at least one DRM (K103N [n = 12, 28%] and M184V [n = 10, 22%] were most commonly detected mutations).","The paper discusses the identification of drug resistance mutations (DRMs) in HIV sequences from patient samples, indicating that HIV sequences were reported from patient samples."
