38031075,15,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, INSTI","In this study, we aimed to assess the degree of viral suppression at different thresholds and treatment duration after the introduction of dolutegravir-based therapy in ten public hospitals in Sierra Leone. Most were women (1,720, 76.3%), had been on ART for more than 24 months (1,434, 63.6%) and were receiving a fixed dose combination of tenofovir, lamivudine and dolutegravir (1705, 75.7%) (Table 1 ).","The paper mentions that the patients were receiving a fixed dose combination of tenofovir (an NRTI), lamivudine (an NRTI), and dolutegravir (an INSTI). It indicates that participants were on NRTIs, while DOL is INSTI, all received drugs belong to NRTI and INSTI classes."
38031075,16,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Tenofovir, Lamivudine, Dolutegravir","Most were women (1,720, 76.3%), had been on ART for more than 24 months (1,434, 63.6%) and were receiving a fixed dose combination of tenofovir, lamivudine and dolutegravir (1705, 75.7%) (Table 1 ). In this study, we aimed to assess the degree of viral suppression at different thresholds and treatment duration after the introduction of dolutegravir-based therapy in ten public hospitals in Sierra Leone","The paper specifies that the participants were receiving a fixed dose combination of tenofovir, lamivudine, and dolutegravir."
38033131,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"Institution based retrospective follow-up study was employed on 492 children and adolescents. Data were collected by trained nurses who have experience working in ART clinics. Data were entered using Epi-data version 4.6 and exported to Stata version 14 for analysis. The proportional hazard assumption was checked, and the Weibull regression was fitted. Cox-Snell residual was used to test the goodness of fit, and the appropriate model was selected by AIC. Finally, an AHR with a 95% CI was computed, and variables with a P-value < 0.05 in the multivariable analysis were taken as significant predictors of virological failure.","The paper does not mention any sequencing of HIV samples from patients. It focuses on the incidence and predictors of virological failure among HIV-infected children and adolescents on first-line antiretroviral therapy in East Shewa hospitals, Oromia Region, Ethiopia. The study is retrospective and involves data collection from medical charts, not from sequencing of biological samples. There is no indication that HIV sequences were obtained or reported in the study. The content discussed analysis and modeling of data related to virological failure, adherence, CD4 counts, and opportunistic infections, but sequencing data or patient samples are not mentioned, therefore, it does not report HIV sequences from patient samples."
38033131,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"ABSTRACT; Infection and predictors of virological failure among HIV infected children and adolescents on first-line antiretroviral therapy in East Shewa hospitals, Oromia Region, Ethiopia: A retrospective follow up study. 2022 J Bacteriol Mycol. All rights reserved.","The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data. It focuses on the incidence and predictors of virological failure among HIV-infected children and adolescents on first-line antiretroviral therapy in East Shewa hospitals, Oromia Region, Ethiopia. The study is retrospective and involves data collection from medical charts, not from in vitro drug susceptibility testing. There is no indication that in vitro drug susceptibility data were obtained or reported in the study. The content discussed analysis and modeling of data related to virological failure, adherence, CD4 counts, and opportunistic infections, but in vitro drug susceptibility testing or data are not mentioned."
