38072961,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,the occurrence of subacute encephalitis caused by CSF drug-resistant HIV escape,"The paper discusses a case study of an HIV-positive patient and includes data on drug resistance mutations in the patient's CSF and plasma HIV samples. This implies that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples, particularly as genetic sequencing methods (Sanger sequencing) were used to identify drug resistance mutations."
38072961,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,No evidence,The content of the paper primarily focuses on a case report of CNS drug-resistant HIV escape and does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing or results. The discussion revolves around clinical observations and treatment adjustments based on genotypic resistance rather than in vitro susceptibility assays.
