38140667,6,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,None,"The study is a comprehensive review of existing literature focused on treatment-emergent resistance to dolutegravir-based regimens in real-world settings. It does not provide any new sequencing data or information on the countries from which samples were obtained, as it is not an original research study but rather a synthesis of previously published data.","The paper is a comprehensive literature review that does not report original research data. It discusses previously published studies on treatment-emergent resistance to dolutegravir-based regimens but does not provide new data on HIV sequences from patient samples. The methods section details how the authors conducted their literature search and data extraction, but there is no mention of obtaining new patient samples or sequencing data from patients in this study. Instead, it focuses on the analysis of existing data from other studies regarding resistance mutations in HIV treated with dolutegravir-based regimens. Therefore, it does not meet the criteria of reporting HIV sequences from patient samples, as no new sequences were generated or shared publically in this review article."
