38864613,9,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"CA, RT",Analysis of CA or RT mutation(s) in the breakthrough viruses from the resistance selection studies was performed using population-based Sanger sequencing at passage 12. Genotypic analysis of wells with virus breakthrough was conducted for the selection experiments starting with M184I RT-encoding virus.,The paper mentions sequencing of the CA and RT regions in the context of resistance selection experiments.
38864613,10,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,Analysis of CA or RT mutation(s) in the breakthrough viruses from the resistance selection studies was performed using population-based Sanger sequencing at passage 12.,The paper mentions the use of population-based Sanger sequencing for analyzing mutations in the resistance selection experiments.
38864613,11,What type of samples were sequenced?,Virus isolates from MT4 cells,"Multiple-cycle antiviral assay in MT4 cells which express green fluorescent protein upon infection (MT4-GFP cells) ISL and LEN were evaluated for their ability to prevent HIV-1 infection in MT4-GFP cells as described in Diamond et al. In this method, HIV-1 replication is monitored using MT4-gag-GFP clone D3, MT4 cells with a GFP reporter gene, the expression of which is dependent on the HIV-1 expressed proteins, Tat and Rev. Infection of MT4-GFP cells with HIV-1 results in GFP expression approximately 24 h post-infection. Proviral variants used for these studies were generated by site-directed mutagenesis in the WT R8 proviral plasmid. Virus was produced by transfection in 293T cells.",The MRCA virus is genomic HIV produced from a 8.5 kb proviral clone transfected into 293T cells -- engineered molecular clone not from patients samples
