36795586,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"We found DTG to be highly effective and safe within our cohort of CALHIV in LMICs. These findings can empower clinicians to prescribe DTG confidently to eligible CALHIV.;""Assessing HIV drug resistance in children and adolescents receiving dolutegravir-based antiretroviral therapy in six countries in Eastern and Southern Africa. (Conflict Of Interest)"" No potential conflict of interest.",The paper does not mention any HIV sequences from patient samples as it focuses on the effectiveness and safety of dolutegravir in children and adolescents living with HIV in various countries in Eastern and Southern Africa.
36795586,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Methods: Retrospective analysis was performed among CALHIV 0–19 years old and weighing greater than or equal to 20 kg who received DTG from 2017 to 2020 at sites in Botswana, Eswatini, Lesotho, Malawi, Tanzania and Uganda to determine effectiveness, safety and predictors of viral load suppression (VLS) among CALHIV using DTG, including through single drug substitutions (SDS).;Results: Among 9419 CALHIV using DTG, 7898 had a documented post-DTG VL, and VLS post-DTG was 93.4% (7378/7898). VLS for antiretroviral therapy (ART) initiations was 92.4% (246/263), and VLS was maintained for the ART-experienced [92.9% (7026/7560) pre- vs. 93.5% (7071/7560) post-DTG; P = 0.14). Among previously unsuppressed, 79.8% (426/534) achieved VLS with DTG. Only 5 patients reported a Grade 3 or 4 adverse event (0.057 per 100 patient-years) requiring DTG discontinuation. History of protease inhibitor-based ART [odds ratio (OR) = 1.53; 95% confidence interval (CI): 1.16–2.03], care in Tanzania (OR = 5.45; 95% CI: 3.41–8.70), and being 15–19 years old (OR = 1.31; 95% CI: 1.03–1.65) were associated with gain of VLS post-DTG. Predictors of VLS on DTG included VLS before DTG (OR = 3.87; 95% CI: 3.03–4.95) and using the once-daily, single tab tenofovir-lamivudine-DTG regimen (OR = 1.78; 95% CI: 1.43–2.22). SDS maintained VLS [95.9% (2032/2120) pre- vs. 95.0% (2014/2120) post-SDS with DTG; P = 0.19], and 83.0% (73/88) of unsuppressed gained VLS using SDS with DTG.",The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data as it primarily discusses the real-world effectiveness and safety of dolutegravir in treating children and adolescents with HIV.
36795586,3,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"We found DTG to be highly effective and safe within our cohort of CALHIV in LMICs. These findings can empower clinicians to prescribe DTG confidently to eligible CALHIV.;""Assessing HIV drug resistance in children and adolescents receiving dolutegravir-based antiretroviral therapy in six countries in Eastern and Southern Africa. (Conflict Of Interest)"" No potential conflict of interest.",The paper does not mention any publicly available sequences related to HIV as it focuses on treatment outcomes rather than genetic sequencing data.
